      "oracle": "Platform-guard contract via Cygwin disagreement scenario: sys.platform='cygwin' and os.name='nt' are both monkeypatched. Correct predicate (sys.platform != 'win32') fires because 'cygwin'!='win32'; wrong predicate (os.name != 'nt') does NOT fire because 'nt'!='nt' is False. With the wrong predicate, the guard is bypassed and connect() proceeds to _open_handle. On Linux CI, kernel32 is not defined (module-level block never ran) so NameError is raised, not ToolError; on Windows, a real pipe open on a non-existent path raises a ToolError whose message does not match 'only supported on Windows'. Either way, pytest.raises fails — making the gate falsifiable on both platforms.",
